    "Spontaneous-blink rates use Noor 1-3 only (one person, ~32 min). The labels do not mark which blinks were voluntary; Noor 2 and 3 contain many close blink pairs (20 and 16 gaps < 0.8 s vs 2 in Noor 1), so if those sessions included a voluntary-blink section, the pooled rate overestimates accidental commands. Noor 1 is the cleanest estimate of natural blinking.",
